  "notes": [
    "CFPB labels come from an LLM (weak labels), not a human. The cfpb_weak_test score measures agreement with that LLM, not correctness. `hand_checked` is against truth built from: the developer's label on every row where a second blind LLM disagreed with the weak label, and the shared label where both LLMs agreed. Rows both LLMs got wrong in the same way are not caught, so it can overstate accuracy.",
    "CFPB narratives are US credit-card complaints; the product sees UK marketplace buyer messages, so the synthetic messages (LLM-written, labelled by construction) are the closest proxy and are easier than real text.",
